#: build-src/community/github.md:1
msgid "GitHub for the NumaHOP user."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:3
msgid ""
"The NumaHOP community principally works on GitHub. An organisation is "
"available for people managing the NumaHOP releases and the documentation. "
"Under the NumaHOP organisation there is 2 active repositories:"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:6
msgid ""
"[github.com/NumaHOP/NumaHOP](https://github.com/NumaHOP/NumaHOP) contains "
"the source code for NumaHOP"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:8
msgid ""
"[github.com/NumaHOP/Documentation](https://github.com/NumaHOP/Documentation) "
"contains the source of the developper manual and the user manual"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:11
msgid "How To Report a Bug"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:13
msgid ""
"If you found a bug inside NumaHop and want to report it you can create an "
"issue on the numahop code repository."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:16
msgid ""
"If you don't have a github account you will need to create one as it is "
"needed to create issues."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:19
msgid ""
"Once logged into github navigate to the NumaHOP "
"[repository](https://github.com/NumaHOP/NumaHOP). Then click on the issue "
"tab to access the list of issues."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:22
msgid "![Issue Tab](../assets/images/issue_tab.jpg)"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:24
msgid ""
"Before creating an issue please spend a bit of time to search existing ones "
"if the bug was already reported."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:27
msgid "Then click on the button labeled **New issue**."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:29
msgid "![New Issue Button](../assets/images/new_issue_btn.jpg)"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:31
msgid "There are 3 options proposed to you:"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:33
msgid "![Issue Choices](../assets/images/issue_choices.jpg)"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:35
msgid ""
"If you are not familiar with the markdown syntax I would advise you to "
"select the **Bug** option. As it propose you to simply fill a form with "
"several questions asked. Otherwise if you know the markdown syntax and are "
"familiar with the information needed inside a bug report you can use the "
"**Blank Issue** option."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:41
msgid "Then fill out the form sections:"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:42
msgid ""
"**Steps to reproduce** should describe the prerequisites and the steps to "
"perform to reproduce the bug."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:44
msgid ""
"**Current Behavior** should describe what is currently happening when the "
"bug is triggered."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:46
msgid ""
"**Expected Behavior** should describe what is you expected should happen "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:48
msgid ""
"**Browser** if the bug is occuring in the interface you must fill out the "
"browser you used when you encountered the bug."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:50
msgid ""
"**Anything else ?** is a section to link additional informations that should "
"be usefull to help resolve the bug."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/community/github.md:53
msgid ""
"Note: you can link files and images (screenshots) by dragging them in any of "
"the textareas."
msgstr ""

